{
  // The large screen, and only the large screen, is checked against the
  // libraries a 2020 television actually has.
  //
  // Both existing guards read the built bundle: one parses it with an ES2017
  // grammar, the other measures it. Neither can see a *runtime* API, because
  // `Object.fromEntries`, `Array.prototype.flat`, `String.prototype.matchAll`
  // and their kind are identifiers, not syntax — they survive the bundler
  // untouched, parse cleanly as ES2017, and then throw on Chromium 68 in
  // somebody's living room. The root configuration offers every workspace
  // `lib: ES2022`, so all of them typechecked.
  //
  // `lib` is what closes that, for ECMAScript builtins. Verified against
  // `Object.fromEntries`, `Array.prototype.flat`, `String.prototype.matchAll`,
  // `String.prototype.replaceAll` and `Array.prototype.at`: every one is a
  // TS2550 here and silent under the root configuration.
  //
  // The root program excludes `apps/tv/src` and `npm run typecheck` runs this
  // project as well, so the screen's own sources are checked exactly once,
  // here. `scripts/typecheck-projects.test.ts` fails if either half of that
  // arrangement is dropped, or if this `lib` is widened.
  //
  // What this does NOT cover, and what no automated check in this repository
  // covers:
  //
  //   - `globalThis`. TypeScript supplies it regardless of `lib`, so it is
  //     silent here exactly as it is under the root configuration — confirmed
  //     by probing `tsc --target ES2017 --lib ES2017,DOM,DOM.Iterable`
  //     directly, as a value and as a type. It arrived in Chrome 71 and the
  //     declared floor is Chromium 68, so it is a real hazard on the oldest
  //     televisions claimed as supported. Nothing catches it. Review does.
  //   - DOM APIs. `lib.dom.d.ts` has no version axis, so a DOM API newer than
  //     the target is invisible to the compiler.
  //
  // The bundle that exists today uses neither, but the guarantee here is
  // "ECMAScript builtins", and it should not be read more widely than that.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2017",
    "lib": ["ES2017", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": [],
    "paths": {
      "@m8/avatars": ["../../packages/avatars/src/index.ts"],
      "@m8/protocol": ["../../packages/protocol/src/index.ts"],
      "@m8/tokens": ["../../packages/tokens/src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
